    "updated_at": "2022-11-14T22:55:05Z",
    "body": "CSS isn't sufficiently well-specified here, but afaict we do intend for \"natural dimensions\" to refer to the density-corrected values. See, for example, https://w3c.github.io/csswg-drafts/css-images-4/#preferred-resolution. And in general we use \"natural dimensions\" when doing things like sizing, which definitely uses the density-corrected values or else it would be nonsensical.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1314513436/reactions",
